WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.660
To all the Halloween-heads out there, you
should probably start following Jamie Lee

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.870
Curtis' social accounts immediately they continue
to be ground zero for glimpses behind the

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:14.900
scenes of the anxiously awaited slasher flicks
Halloween Kills and Halloween Ends.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.280
"Happy Halloween!"

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.900
The iconic scream queen, who portrays Laurie
Strode in the Halloween franchise, has been

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.529
quite busy on her socials since Halloween
Kills officially kicked off production in

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:27.519
September 2019.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:32.961
So far, Curtis' posts have largely been still
shots taken on set or in her trailer, like

00:00:32.961 --> 00:00:35.149
this Instagram post, which Curtis captioned,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.040
"NEVER SAY DIE!

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.880
First day back in the battle for my life!"

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.710
It appears the spooky time of year has the
Halloween Kills star in the sharing mood,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:50.501
though, as Curtis recently took to Twitter
to offer Halloween fans a tasty treat: a 21-second

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:55.250
video that marks the first in-motion look
at Halloween Kills.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.250
Curtis tweeted,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.299
"‘Tis the season..... to start screaming.

00:00:59.299 --> 00:01:02.660
First look at the mayhem David has created
for all of you."

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.930
Needless to say, but it appears a bloody bad
time is in store for the Strode clan in the

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.840
upcoming sequel to 2018's Halloween.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:17.120
Penned by David Gordon Green, Danny McBride,
and Jeff Fradley and directed by Green himself,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:23.050
2018's Halloween served as a direct follow-up
to John Carpenter's legendary slasher classic

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.430
of the same name from 1978.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.869
Set a few decades after the events of Carpenter's
Halloween, the 2018 movie found Laurie Strode

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:36.299
a little older, a lot grayer, and so deeply
traumatized by her encounter with knife-wielding

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:41.330
psychopath Michael Myers that she'd spent
the ensuing years drinking her pain away while

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:46.590
training herself and her family for a second
showdown with the one we've come to call "The

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.590
Shape."

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:52.200
That showdown indeed came in the blood-spattered
madness of Green's Halloween.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.800
When it happened, Laurie and company eventually
trapped the murderous Myers inside a burning

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.800
house.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.770
Of course, Michael Myers isn't that easy to
kill.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:05.820
The basement cage clearly didn't hold, since
the grisly gang is back for a pair of sequels

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.349
that will end the saga of Laurie Strode and
Michael Myers.

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:14.670
Now a couple of weeks into filming, Halloween
Kills is the first of those expected sequels

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.650
and if Curtis' teaser is any indication, things
are heating up on set.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:23.340
Like, literally heating up, as it appears
the Halloween Kills team has already shot

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.540
Michael's escape from the burning basement.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.709
At one point in the video, Michael is seen
standing on the porch of Laurie's house, fire

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:36.319
ablaze behind him, with what appears to be
a torrential downpour (or perhaps firefighter's

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:39.470
water hoses) damping the raging flames.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.680
If you're wondering what this video might
reveal about the horrors Laurie and her family

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.690
are facing in Halloween Kills, well, there's
really not that much we can glean from it.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.409
As of the making of this video, the plots
to both Halloween Kills and Halloween Ends

00:02:53.409 --> 00:02:55.470
are being kept under wraps.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:59.970
While Green and McBride have both been candid
about their sequels bringing an end to the

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:04.420
Laurie Strode-Michael Myers saga, they have
categorically refused to tip their hands as

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:09.330
to whether either character will make it out
alive, or if they'll both meet their ultimate

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.330
dooms.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:16.530
Clearly, Laurie underestimated Michael's mortality
in 2018's Halloween as she did on two separate

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:19.049
occasions as a teen in the original movie.

00:03:19.049 --> 00:03:23.200
That means in the coming sequels she'll likely
be forced to reckon with the notion that her

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.970
decades of prep may have been for naught.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:29.159
We can only hope she's got a backup plan to
deal with Michael.

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:33.880
For now, all we can really do is hope that
David Gordon Green and the Halloween Kills

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.830
and Halloween Ends crew are bringing as much
fire and fury to the sequels as they did to

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.450
the 2018 flick.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.629
We'll get our first look at those sequels
in a little under a year's time, when Halloween

00:03:44.629 --> 00:03:50.810
Kills hits theaters on October 16, 2020 with
Halloween Ends arriving almost exactly a year

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.689
later on October 15, 2021.

00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:58.610
Until then, stay tuned to Looper and Jamie
Lee Curtis' social media accounts, evidently

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.280
for updates on Halloween Kills.

